        "id": 130990,
        "name": "phantaskippy",
        "username": "phantaskippy",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/phantaskippy/{size}/1897_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T15:50:06.000Z",
        "cooked": "<p>Which is actually less difficult that requiring all 4 shuffle cards in the trash at the same time.</p><p>Not that it isn't incredibly rare, but there are ways it can happen. &nbsp;The key is all devices need to be accounted for by being in the trash, in play or played by traps mid-chain for any of them to happen. &nbsp;The 4 shuffle cards have to be dealt with, but they don't have to start in the trash, but even if they were all in the trash to start, you don't have a loop until the devices are dealt with, which mid-loop should be harder to get rid of.</p><p>The odds are still really, really low, and then only for a non-balanced challenge mode.</p><p>&nbsp;</p>",
        "post_number": 21,
        "post_type": 1,
        "updated_at": "2021-02-07T04:06:13.184Z",
