      {
        "id": 130991,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T15:54:18.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>Yeah, all you need is him having 10 specific cards not in his deck, playing 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and for that card to reveal 4 more very specific cards before finding a trap.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Which can be simplified to: remove 10 specific cards from his deck and play 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and INEVITABLY play the other traps in his deck over and over until death or other infinite cycles.</p>\n<p>Yes, it's difficult to pull off. We know. But it's there.</p>",
