        "id": 130992,
        "name": "Foote",
        "username": "Foote",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/foote/{size}/1877_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T16:01:51.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Yeah, all you need is him having 10 specific cards not in his deck, playing 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and for that card to reveal 4 more very specific cards before finding a trap.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWhich can be simplified to: remove 10 specific cards from his deck and play 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and INEVITABLY play the other traps in his deck over and over until death or other infinite cycles.Yes, it's difficult to pull off. We know. But it's there.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>It's an unbalanced play mode used to up the challenge. Even though it could happen, I'm not sold that this is a huge deal all things considered</p>",
