      {
        "id": 130993,
        "name": "Ronway",
        "username": "Ronway",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/{size}/1856_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T16:04:39.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote no-group\" data-username=\"xThe Killswitch\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n xThe Killswitch:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\n<div><b>Ronway wrote:</b><br><blockquote>Yeah, all you need is him having 10 specific cards not in his deck, playing 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and for that card to reveal 4 more very specific cards before finding a trap.\n&nbsp;\n</blockquote></div>\nWhich can be simplified to: remove 10 specific cards from his deck and play 1 of 2 cards remaining in his 15 card deck, and INEVITABLY play the other traps in his deck over and over until death or other infinite cycles.\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>By getting rid of the line I made, you no longer have Quick Stim Patch and Run and Gun accounted for. By not factoring them in, you have now opened up the door to when one of the traps are on top of the deck, that when it reshuffles and places a card, that it plays one of those two cards, this will reshuffle the trash back into the deck, bringing all devices back with it.&nbsp;</p>",
