      {
        "id": 130994,
        "name": "Killswitch",
        "username": "Killswitch",
        "avatar_template": "/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/killswitch/{size}/2116_2.png",
        "created_at": "2015-02-10T16:43:10.000Z",
        "cooked": "<aside class=\"quote group-playtesters\" data-username=\"Ronway\">\n<div class=\"title\">\n<div class=\"quote-controls\"></div>\n<img loading=\"lazy\" alt=\"\" width=\"24\" height=\"24\" src=\"https://forums.greaterthangames.com/user_avatar/forums.greaterthangames.com/ronway/48/1856_2.png\" class=\"avatar\"> Ronway:</div>\n<blockquote>\n<p>By getting rid of the line I made, you no longer have Quick Stim Patch and Run and Gun accounted for. By not factoring them in, you have now opened up the door to when one of the traps are on top of the deck, that when it reshuffles and places a card, that it plays one of those two cards, this will reshuffle the trash back into the deck, bringing all devices back with it.</p>\n</blockquote>\n</aside>\n<p>Oh okay. Well, it would be easier to pull it off by somehow discarding those four reshuffles before they were played then.</p>\n<p>I wouldn't say most challenges are unbalanced, but this one seems to be particularly so just because he's Ambuscade.</p>",
